+## Usage metadata
+
+Each completed provider request appends a `rpiv-btw:usage:v1` custom session entry.
+The entry contains `version: 1`, a unique `id`, `source: "btw"`, `provider`,
+`model`, and the provider's `usage` object. `usage` includes input, output, cache
+read, cache write and total tokens, plus the corresponding cost fields. Values
+are preserved exactly as Pi reports them, including zero values. Questions,
+answers, prompts and context are excluded.
+
+A context-overflow retry produces a separate entry for each completed request.
+Responses with an error or aborted stop reason also produce entries. A rejected
+request without a response cannot report usage. After session replacement or
+shutdown, late responses are discarded so they cannot modify another session.
+
+The main conversation's usage totals are unchanged. Extensions can read these
+custom entries and display side-request usage separately.
